microspice @PROJECT_VERSION@ - desktop test package

Project source: https://github.com/michaelnwanna/microspice

Action icons are rendered from lucide-static 0.468.0 by Lucide Contributors,
with portions derived from Feather by Cole Bemis. The complete ISC/Feather
license is included as licenses/Lucide-LICENSE.txt.
Upstream: https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide

This package dynamically links Qt @Qt6_VERSION@. Qt libraries and plugins are
provided by The Qt Company and other contributors. The qt-sbom directory
contains the available SPDX documents from the exact SDK used to build this
package, including component attribution and license expressions. These SDK
documents can also cover components not shipped in this package. They are
provenance materials, not a complete deployed-binary license audit.

Qt source archives: https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/
Qt licensing: https://www.qt.io/licensing/open-source-lgpl-obligations

The licenses directory includes unmodified LGPLv3 and GPLv3 companion texts
from https://github.com/qt/qtbase/tree/v6.8.3/LICENSES. Qt versions used by this
project have LGPLv3 license options for the linked Core/Gui/Widgets modules.
The SDK SBOMs identify additional third-party terms that still require review.

Qt is not statically linked into microspice. This test package does not prohibit
replacement of its Qt shared libraries with compatible modified versions, or
reverse engineering for debugging such modifications. Platform code signing
may require re-signing a modified application before it can be launched.

Windows packages also include Microsoft Visual C++ and Universal C Runtime
redistributable libraries, subject to the applicable Microsoft Visual Studio
license and redistribution terms, not Qt's licenses.

